# Line endings.
#
# This repository ships shell scripts that are executed by bash inside Termux,
# on Android. A CRLF script does not fail subtly there: bash reads the carriage
# return as part of the last token on every line and the run dies with
# `$'\r': command not found`, `syntax error near unexpected token $'{\r'`, and
# an `umask: 077: octal number out of range` from the very first lines.
#
# The blobs in this repository are LF and must stay LF. Without this file, a
# Windows checkout converts them on the way out, every one of them shows up as
# a whole-file diff, and committing from that checkout would publish scripts
# that cannot run on the device the plugin exists for. The same conversion is
# what has been keeping LICENSE permanently "modified".
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means: decide text vs binary by content, and check text
# out with LF on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the files where getting this wrong is fatal rather than
# cosmetic: the three scripts that run in Termux, and the test that runs them.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Build output and images are compared byte for byte by CI; never touch them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jar binary
